 {:db/id "q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "531e02f0-754c-57e9-98aa-5097314bafb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec/29cacc3eb3ebb780bf8ddab721070ad619576e26c2fc61c64446a322f523b1d7" "q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec/44115e60d44876fed7a97791025c484665e5094940057cb5c4fba998fe1f7fa1" "q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec/39032852c93506841040cea210c246307611dc4cacc74bd3393aff1102b1bd08" "q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec/01b05e54253f0dbbde8e2bdf8433c7bcaabc4214bf9f64e7cc15490b6e916ccc" "q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec/0a7693dc2eb2301b9e10131ed55fc8dddc41f381d4866f5f2e1feb343184dbae"] :answer-field/correct "q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec/39032852c93506841040cea210c246307611dc4cacc74bd3393aff1102b1bd08" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161902" :question/id #uuid "f21c0998-8903-5ed2-945d-a8c8324dedb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161902" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=⟨0,\\,y,\\,-x⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the cone $z=3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9$ and the plane $z=y-x.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=y-x$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper plane ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-x)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-x)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=y,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot (-1)-y\\cdot 1+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider lower cone ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9)=\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9)=\\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=y,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot \\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y\\cdot \\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161902/ma-source-field/218a0876ff27b5f8f1059f2aac08b27c3219a4d8c2e226e96e5df808632946ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
