 {:db/id "q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c61b134-7c57-530f-8b97-97a808179f81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e/dd762800f4b71cfafc03662548916d68dbfe7fc645fbe2019a9af6ad5738f7b5" "q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e/8677dcad2796c7847060059caa312c0dfa2665951f055ec29033de0f5d36c9d2" "q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e/a30e3ca7171eb8f8979bcbc8f4bd8b1ecdeb2dd995a3386eb72f35596734f2e3" "q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e/b3a3c43910377f00d2e0b238bd1134acb656e47cc8367c78291a9a72b2746142" "q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e/e96136247234b0f813925d22f6f73bd9fd8c551e2dd77281449fdcf929745736"] :answer-field/correct "q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e/a30e3ca7171eb8f8979bcbc8f4bd8b1ecdeb2dd995a3386eb72f35596734f2e3" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-162517" :question/id #uuid "6d5fedbb-f6c9-5abe-b595-3219e3d242a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-162517" :question/problem "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y\\,i-2x{y}^{2}\\,j?$" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y\\,i-2x{y}^{2}\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y$ and $Q(x,y)=-2x{y}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=4xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-4xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=4xy+(-4xy)=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}=2{x}^{2}y,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}=2x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}=(xy)^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162517/ma-source-field/fc63579ff4b5b807a48594d500e60507e070505ef5ff0ba1acf54ea8a643a50e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
