 {:db/id "q-162633" :question/id #uuid "66bd138c-5fd7-52b5-b1a8-7c242f9884ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-162633" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ , $t\\ne n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162633/ma-source-field/df868966dcfadd561b6189b8d3394b19bed0ddb7804956c4fe1809726b4193fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
