 {:db/id "q-162637" :question/id #uuid "7adf6f23-c582-5c46-b1a7-7edbfe6210af" :question/math-academy-id "q-162637" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-{t}^{3})\\,i+3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-{t}^{3}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162637/ma-source-field/f5a7b905656635bdfd9bd85b1f481c63fa34fa3fba67f2a2824bc7dfaf075973"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
