 {:db/id "q-164401" :question/id #uuid "98ad452f-818a-5095-bf60-3f83ccbaae0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-164401" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =4\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $x=2$ and $x=6$ in the $xz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164401/ma-source-field/361940a79bb3d248d264cb04e3b00013d52cbfc4c036762c18544c6a112dc5c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
