 {:db/id "q-164403" :question/id #uuid "1ef46611-6066-5608-b7b6-cb53d9ef1a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-164403" :question/problem "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand an ellipsoid centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an ellipsoid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-2,0),\\,a=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{7},\\,c=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164403/ma-source-field/b7ae01d24f5921f71299c56cdb5b42fa563c3c3c275530e80b3fd586ef080680"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
