 {:db/id "q-164417" :question/id #uuid "1a066ac1-6120-502f-9195-eb35e4541908" :question/math-academy-id "q-164417" :question/problem "What is the domain in the $xy$-plane of the hyperbolic cylinder $(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The full expression describing all points on our hyperbolic cylinder is\n\n$$\n(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,\\,z=k\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in R$ can vary arbitrarily. \n\nThe domain of any cylinder in the $xy$-plane is its base curve. Hence, in this case, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }(x+5)^{2}-{y}^{2}=1}.\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola centered at $(-5,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164417/ma-source-field/68ce3e3c2d4612fd7d52c653c260a6b83a11e152c14ee6aef7be45e36f0373fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
