 {:db/id "q-164477" :question/id #uuid "37f3129a-ae32-5711-8b8d-cb83602d7d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164477" :question/problem "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cylinder centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an elliptic cylinder with $a=b=\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164477/ma-source-field/377378540789f7f3b422fd1323ece696bcdb16f441cdd042362fa35a79766e6d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
