 {:db/id "q-164479" :question/id #uuid "7a3947ec-3744-5af7-8ce2-1be319e6d154" :question/math-academy-id "q-164479" :question/problem "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder with $a=3,\\,b=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-164479/ma-source-field/66a9cfc074f6922ce1069e96e95aab79a4834f48a03864c73e4b0dea208632d4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
