 {:db/id "q-164547" :question/id #uuid "50443007-c819-5285-a74f-1d6dfd323e6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164547" :question/problem "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=2z,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4pz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis and $p=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164547/ma-source-field/3ce1a22bda5a5399a319328e0bbcbd73202e8afd161caf89a1566c25d11acc1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
