 {:db/id "q-164553" :question/id #uuid "040e9acf-1af9-5813-86f6-e469cb0eecc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-164553" :question/problem "Identify the surface $5{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}+20x+10z+15=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}+20x+10z+15 & =0 \\\\ 5({x}^{2}+4x)-{y}^{2}-5({z}^{2}-2z)+15 & =0 \\\\ 5[(x+2)^{2}-4]-{y}^{2}-5[(z-1)^{2}-1]+15 & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}-20-{y}^{2}-5(z-1)^{2}+5+15 & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}-{y}^{2}-5(z-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ -5(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+5(z-1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164553/ma-source-field/a38f8228a5460da06e54a473f9346e8a5883fe4804a25a5009d16a5c60761e35"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
